@startuml pipeline-java
' Hand-maintained. Source of truth = .github/workflows/master-java-pipeline.yml + java-verify.yml + java-release.yml
title Java pipeline — template pattern, three levels of workflow_call, one of two entry points

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

package "consumer repo" as CALLER #EEEEEE {
  [.github/workflows/ci.yml] as CI <<caller>>
}

[master-java-pipeline.yml] as M <<workflow_call>> #FFFFFF

package "① build + verify — every job starts at t=0" as S1 #E8F0FE {
  [java-build.yml] as B <<test-compile · reject .env>>
  package "java-verify.yml — grouping only, no steps" as V #E6F4EA {
    [java-lint.yml] as L
    [java-unit-tests.yml] as U
    [java-integration-tests.yml] as I
    [java-security.yml] as SEC <<CodeQL · Gitleaks · Trivy>>
  }
}

[java-dependency-graph.yml] as DG <<push events only>> #E8F0FE

package "② java-release.yml — grouping only, no steps" as S2 #FEF7E0 {
  [tag.yml] as T <<PRs to main>>
  [java-docker.yml] as D <<buildpack · scan · SBOM · sign>>
  [deploy-gitops.yml] as G <<verify gate · bump manifest>>
}

[build-gate] as GATE <<if: always()>> #FFF3C4

CI --> M : uses: @<sha>\nsecrets: inherit
M --> B
M --> V
M --> DG
M --> S2

B --> DG : needs
B --> S2 : needs
V --> S2 : needs
D --> G : needs\n+ image-digest output

B ..> GATE
DG ..> GATE
V ..> GATE
S2 ..> GATE

note top of M
  **Template pattern, not orchestrator.**
  Every arrow is a uses: reference GitHub's
  scheduler resolves — nothing dispatches a
  workflow and polls it. So each leaf is its
  own status check, permissions intersect
  downward, and no PAT is involved.

  build-gate aggregates results but drives
  nothing: it is a gate, not a controller.

  Depth: caller → master → grouping → leaf
  = 4 of the 10 levels GitHub allows.
end note

note right of S1
  **verify has NO needs: build.**
  Nothing in it consumes build's output —
  every job checks out and compiles for
  itself, so all five start at t=0.
end note

note right of DG
  Its own workflow, not a job in java-build.yml:
  • keeps build at contents: read
    (only graph submission needs write)
  • stays off the critical path — a needs:
    on a reusable workflow waits for EVERY
    job inside it
end note

note bottom of GATE
  **permissions: {} — needs nothing.**
  Fails only on failure/cancelled;
  "skipped" is a pass (dependency-graph is
  push-only, release jobs skip per event).
end note

note bottom of S2
  **tag.yml and deploy-gitops.yml are shared
  with master-python-pipeline.yml** — they are
  language-agnostic, so neither has a java- prefix
  and neither may be forked per language.

  Event gating (java-release.yml):
  • tag          — PR → main, same-repo only
  • docker-publish — push, or same-repo PR
    (PR builds are NOT pushed or signed)
  • deploy-gitops  — push to refs/heads/main
end note

footer docs/pipeline-java.puml — Bigorno12/ci-cd-templates
@enduml
